  <h2>How the \"Rolling 5-Hour Window\" Works</h2>
  <p>Unlike Alibaba's explicit weekly credit cap (40k credits/7 days), Anthropic uses a <strong>rolling 5-hour window</strong>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Capacity is measured over the last 5 hours of activity</li>
    <li>No weekly bucket, no rollover, no Sunday reset</li>
    <li>A burst at 2 PM affects capacity at 6 PM; by 8 PM it's recovered</li>
    <li>\"Weekly limit\" is a derived metric: (5h capacity) × (active hours per week) / 5</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This means <strong>there is no weekly limit</strong> — only a sustained-rate limit. An engineer who codes 10 hours/day, 5 days/week gets ~10× the 5-hour capacity per week. One who codes 2 hours/day gets ~2×.</p>

