  <h2>FinOps Recommendation</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Default to Max 5x ($100)</strong> for every engineer coding daily with AI.</li>
    <li><strong>Monitor for 30 days:</strong> Track throttle events/week and API overflow spend per engineer.</li>
    <li><strong>Upgrade selectively:</strong> Move only engineers meeting all three upgrade signals to Max 20x.</li>
    <li><strong>Cap Max 20x at 20–30% of seats.</strong> A 10-person team needs at most 2–3 Max 20x seats.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep API budget separate.</strong> Subscriptions cover interactive only; automation needs API budget.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Bottom Line</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Max 5x = $100/mo for daily coding.</strong> Pays for itself if it saves 2 hrs/mo at $50/hr.</li>
    <li><strong>Max 20x = $200/mo for burst refactoring.</strong> Justified only when throttles cost >$100/mo in lost productivity.</li>
    <li><strong>No weekly limits exist.</strong> Capacity is a rolling 5-hour rate, not a weekly bucket.</li>
    <li><strong>Shared pool = contention risk.</strong> Don't put all Max 20x seats on one team/repo.</li>
  </ul>